{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And the king of the south shall engage him in battle</b> — this is Egypt, and there is no concern that Egypt would be of whatever religion it may be." "<b>And the king of the north shall storm against him</b> — against the king of Egypt, like (Nahum 1:3) 'in the storm and in the whirlwind.' And if it is written with shin, like השירו, I do not know, and many are so."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra notes a variant spelling of ויתנגח/וישתער or its root with shin vs. sin; the reference to השירו is obscure and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:22.179758510Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}